{"data": {"id": "EPA-HQ-OW-2022-0114-1811", "type": "comments", "links": {"self": "https://api.regulations.gov/v4/comments/EPA-HQ-OW-2022-0114-1811"}, "attributes": {"commentOn": "0900006485883ec6", "commentOnDocumentId": "EPA-HQ-OW-2022-0114-0027", "duplicateComments": 15851, "address1": null, "address2": null, "agencyId": "EPA", "city": null, "category": null, "comment": "See attached file(s)<br/><br/>Dear Administrator Regan,<br/><br/>Attached are a total of 15,851 individual comments submitted by advocates and supporters of the National Wildlife Federation Action Fund in support of the Environmental Protection Agency&rsquo;s proposed drinking water standards to provide long overdue federal protections against six types of highly toxic PFAS.<br/><br/>The PFAS crisis is widespread, contaminating the blood of humans, fish, and wildlife worldwide. Communities of color and low-income communities are particularly impacted by PFAS exposure, where health impacts are often compounded because these communities tend to face cumulative effects from multiple environmental injustices and public health hazards.<br/><br/>We urge the Environmental Protection Agency to move swiftly to finalize health-protective standards to reduce PFAS in our drinking water. Thank you for your consideration and for your work to address our nation&rsquo;s PFAS crisis.", "country": null, "displayProperties": [{"name": "pageCount", "label": "Page Count", "tooltip": "Number of pages In the content file"}], "docAbstract": null, "docketId": "EPA-HQ-OW-2022-0114", "documentType": "Public Submission", "email": null, "fax": null, "field1": null, "field2": null, "fileFormats": null, "firstName": null, "govAgency": null, "govAgencyType": null, "objectId": "0900006485a8c1c1", "lastName": null, "legacyId": null, "modifyDate": "2023-06-05T14:06:39Z", "organization": null, "originalDocumentId": null, "pageCount": 1, "phone": null, "postedDate": "2023-06-05T04:00:00Z", "postmarkDate": "2023-05-30T04:00:00Z", "re